Empty pairs are text: {//} {**} {__} {~~} {^^} {,,} {==} {++} {##}.\n -> text.carve
\n -> text.carve
A pair that holds something is the construct:  -> text.carve
{/ -> text.carve markup.italic.carve keyword.control.italic.carve
i -> text.carve markup.italic.carve markup.italic.carve
/} -> text.carve markup.italic.carve keyword.control.italic.carve
  -> text.carve
{* -> text.carve markup.bold.carve keyword.control.bold.carve
b -> text.carve markup.bold.carve markup.bold.carve
*} -> text.carve markup.bold.carve keyword.control.bold.carve
  -> text.carve
{~ -> text.carve markup.deleted.carve keyword.control.strike.carve
s -> text.carve markup.deleted.carve markup.deleted.carve
~} -> text.carve markup.deleted.carve keyword.control.strike.carve
  -> text.carve
{+ -> text.carve markup.inserted.critic.carve keyword.control.critic.carve
ins -> text.carve markup.inserted.critic.carve markup.inserted.carve
+} -> text.carve markup.inserted.critic.carve keyword.control.critic.carve
  -> text.carve
{# -> text.carve comment.block.critic.carve keyword.control.critic.carve
 c  -> text.carve comment.block.critic.carve comment.block.content.carve
#} -> text.carve comment.block.critic.carve keyword.control.critic.carve
.\n -> text.carve
